  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 26. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 慣習 — 長い間繰り返されてきた生活などの習わし。\n2. 肝臓 — 栄養を蓄えたり体に不要な物を処理したりする臓器。\n3. 寒暖計 — 気温などを測る温度計。\n4. 勘違い — 間違って思い込むこと。\n5. 貫通 — 一方から反対側まで突き抜けること。\n6. 完売 — 用意した品物が全部売れること。\n7. 間伐 — 林を育てるために一部の木を間引くこと。\n8. 寒波 — 広い地域に押し寄せる強い寒さ。\n9. 完敗 — 力を十分に出せず大きく負けること。\n10. 看病 — 病気の人のそばで世話をすること。\n11. 巻末 — 本のいちばん後ろの部分。\n12. 甘味料 — 食べ物などに甘さを加えるもの。\n13. 冠 — 身分や栄誉などを示すために頭にかぶる飾り。\n14. 寛容 — 違いや失敗などを広い心で受け止めること。\n15. 慣用句 — 二つ以上の言葉が結びついて特別な意味を持つ言い方。\n16. 管理者 — 場所や仕組みなどを整えて守る責任を持つ人。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\n",
